The loop executes once for each element in each test input list, so summing the 18 list lengths gives 47 total iterations. The invariant fails exactly when `sanitized_parts` contains some string ending in `.`, and from the function body that can only happen via the `part == '..'` branch, because that branch may append the literal `'..'` or preserve an earlier `'..'`; the regex branch instead rewrites trailing dots/spaces to `#`, so it cannot introduce a dot-ending element. Counting post-iteration states across the 18 concrete test inputs where `'..'` is present in `sanitized_parts` gives 13 violating snapshots, so the invariant is not always true.

